  "rule": "In English, a question about someone uses does and keeps the person in the middle: Where does Vale live?\n\nSpanish drops does and puts the person after the verb:\n\nquestion word + verb + person\n*¿Dónde vive Vale?*\n*¿Cuándo llegan los clientes?*\n\nPutting the person first, *¿Dónde Vale vive?*, sounds foreign straight away.\n\nYes/no questions are relaxed. You can keep the normal order and let the *¿ ?* and your voice do the work: *¿Vale vive aquí? ¿Vive Vale aquí?* Both are fine.\n\nIn answers, the new information goes last:\n*¿Quién llega a las siete?*\n*Llega don Hernando.*",
  "smallPrint": "Spanish puts the subject after the verb in question-word questions (inversion).",
  "readAndPick": [
    {
      "es": "¿Dónde trabaja Mariana?",
      "options": [
        "Where does Mariana work?",
        "Where do you work, Mariana?",
        "Does Mariana work?"
